{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/77438-big-bad-wolf","id":77438,"title":"Big Bad Wolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-22T18:32:59-08:00","id":77438,"title":"Big Bad Wolf","content":"Can anyone give me pointers on scenarios to have a big bad wolf/ little red riding hood as an NPC in a game? I have the beast rolled up, and I want her to be flirty, but a little menacing. I am running a kind of mystery game, I just want ideas for what to have her do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T20:29:04-08:00","id":77456,"title":"","content":"Would you clarify &quot;big bad wolf/little red riding hood&quot; a bit? It may matter slightly if you mean to draw on the role the Big Bad Wolf plays in Little Red Riding Hood for inspiration, or if the character is actually a sort of composite of the wolf and Red.<br /> <br /> Actually, nah, I'll mostly play with the latter; I don't see any particular options for discussion open up from the former alone. So, just lobbing out possibilities (spoilered for space) :<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> - She may be heavily motivated by a family member, or someone like family to her (Granny, or someone like her). Likewise, she may be using someone else so motivated to accomplish her goals (Wolf). Both, to one degree or another, even where &quot;Granny&quot; is the same person in both cases.<br /> - In addition to flirty and menacing, she may be truly mostly innocent (Red). Though she may also give a hint that she isn't completely so (Wolf). May in fact be completely innocent or as far from it as possible, while giving the impression of the opposite.<br /> - She may have few concerns with following the rules or otherwise doing what people tell her, even knowing the danger (Red). She may instead (or in addition) be all too glad to take advantage of others doing likewise (Wolf).<br /> - There may have been a status quo up until recently, with the character either being victimized or otherwise in a tight spot (Red) or doing spectacular and/or about to get away with it (Wolf). And then along came a &quot;Huntsman,&quot; someone or something that miraculously bails the character out or threatens to screw everything up if action isn't taken.<br /> - The character may be taken in by (Red) or be (Wolf) someone under a false identity, if not carrying out an outright impersonation. Though it certainly could be, this needn't necessarily be maliciously done, whether simply carried out as a matter of convenience/desperation or even benevolence (doesn't strictly follow inspiration from the fairy tale, but could be a bit of a twist if the players think they can follow the fairy tale connections). The false identity or impersonation may also be varying degrees of flimsy (&quot;What big ears you have!&quot;) and the defense perhaps more effective than it should be (&quot;Why, the better to hear you with!&quot;).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Further, while maybe a bit removed from what you want, elements from or references to other fairy tales/stories using wolves or the Big Bad Wolf could be fun, if they catch your fancy:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">* The Boy Who Cried Wolf - she or others (the Boy) give false warnings about something (possibly her, in the latter case) to the PCs/others and/or her. It gets some preparation and then proves false twice (&quot;I've got a hot tip they're gonna hit this place, tonight at 11 PM!&quot;), before proving true a third time with no such prepared response. Or maybe this happened recently, and she's dealing with/profiting from the aftermath.<br /> * The Dog and the Wolf - another character (the Dog; need not be an actual dog Beast Changeling) is in a more secure circumstance than hers, but a less free one. She's derisive of this (Wolf). She may, however, have to deal with it (e.g. the Dog is actually a friend/relative she wants to help; or her own circumstances are bad enough that she's tempted to take/look it up herself).<br /> * The Wolf and the Crane - she helps or is helped (the Crane) by another character to get out of a tight spot, at no small risk to the helper. The payment she receives or gives is simply not to push an advantage the helped gained over the helper as a result of the helping. (e.g. &quot;Thank you for breaking in there and saving my son. In return, I will not sell knowledge of the crime you committed to do it to a blackmailer.&quot;) Bitter feelings may simmer afterwards on either side.<br /> * The Three Little Pigs - eh, kinda running outta steam. The Pigs (as with the Dog and Crane, need not be Beast Changelings, amusing an option though it is) as three somewhat similar friends/relatives (two relative slackers next to a third) could just kinda be around, and players might make the connection quick enough. Could be characters whose lives she's destroyed (possibly except #3, who may or may not be the sole survivor); but could just be former relationships that didn't work out but ended in varying degrees of amiability, the third of which may still be happening (could work with the flirty angle, too), or even just friends, family, co-workers, or people she knows.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Naturally, you probably don't want to use <i>all</i> of these at once. You also may want to dial back some or all of them if you do use them, depending on what you want. It depends on how overt you want the fairy tale connections to be: as pointed out in the fifth point, players might pick up on them and try to use what they know of the story. This could be exactly what you want, or something you don't want to seem obvious until after the fact, or you may just want is a kind of thematic element, not a &quot;big thing.&quot; Still, potential fun to be had if connections are so obvious the Freehold gossips about them, possibly with amusement/disquiet.* ... Yes, I'm aware I may have constructed things a bit too elaborately for a mystery game, but hey, the idea train kinda ran away with me. &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> * Just running with the Three Little Pigs thing...<br /> &quot;Oh, no, she's going out with <i>the third</i> Swanson Brother, now? Jeez. Heh, well, here's hoping this little piggy makes his house with bricks when she goes huffing and puffing. If you know what I mean.&quot;<br /> &quot;... Izzat a sexual metaphor?&quot;<br /> &quot;What? ... Ew, no! I meant when she gets flirty with other guys! I meant when she maybe blows down <i>the relationship</i>, not when she blows <i>hi</i>-- Ugh...&quot;<br /> &quot;... So I take it you're not gonna finish that muffin. Mind if I, uh...?&quot;<br /> &quot;You may not.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 02-22-2014, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T20:35:15-08:00","id":78027,"title":"","content":"I actually like a lot of the ideas you suggested, and will probably use at least one or two of them. My original inspiration was a collection of Little Red Riding Hood pictures titled &quot;Wolfsbane and Mistletoe&quot; and I started thinking about doing some kind of love spell scenario, but quickly realized I couldn't make it work. (My party is consisted of all couples in real life, and the wife of one couple and husband of another are very jealous of anyone getting close to their significant other, even in a joking way.) So these ideas actually helped me quite a bit and gave me jumping off points for other ideas of my own. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T06:24:51-08:00","id":78270,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear my rambling was helpful to you. ^_^ I had a lot of fun with the brainstorming exercise, so thanks for the prompt.<br /> <br /> If you feel like sharing, I'd love to hear what you ultimately do with her and how the game winds up going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T12:12:22-08:00","id":78489,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sure thing! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not sure when I'll be running my game again, my boyfriend has a simultaneous one going on so we take turns on the weekends, but hopefully it'll be this weekend or next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T19:11:19-08:00","id":79852,"title":"","content":"Watch Trick R Treat! Do the Anna Paquin character as a beastie Autumn courtier that does a yearly human eating party every Halloween with the local Scarecrow Ministry composed of maiden theme Beasties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T16:19:41-08:00","id":81300,"title":"","content":"I can't actually watch horror movies ^_^;; Not even remotely scary ones...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}